No one is born a trader; it's just that your starting point is higher. If you come in swinging with hundreds of thousands, you're not in the rookie phase anymore, and the cost of mistakes is steeper. But at the core, it's all the same. Once you hit a certain level of losses, you either walk away for good or learn how to trade; 

Using the wrong strategies and ending up with good results can cloud your judgment on whether it's skill or just luck. In the beginner phase, all you get are negative feedback loops, and eventually, you'll find your way to real certainty. You either push yourself to quit or push yourself to learn; 

So, I don’t recommend getting too comfortable right off the bat. Bad habits are easy to form, but good ones take time to cultivate. 
